 and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Unreal Past: Hypothetical but Probable Situation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about the unreal past, you use past tenses to talk about hypothetical situations and possible results in the present. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Type 2 Conditional</span> to refer to a hypothetical situation that could lead to a probable result.<br/> The <span class=\"strong\">Type 2 Conditional</span> is used to refer to a condition that is in the present. The situation that results from this condition is not certain to be real.<br/><br/> Structure:<br/> If+ subject + Simple Past, subject + Present Conditional<br/><br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I felt better, I'<span class=\"strong\">d</span> come to work.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The condition of feeling better is not guaranteed, but it is a possibility.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If fender benders didn't happen, we <span class=\"strong\">would </span>never be late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We<span class=\"strong\"> would</span> miss out on big corporate paydays if staff didn't come to work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you called in before your shift began, we<span class=\"strong\"> would</span> have time to find someone to take your shift. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you guys weren't late so often we <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> be in this mess.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you had called me, we<span class=\"strong\"> wouldn't</span> be having this conversation.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Time Clauses: Every Time, Once, Before, Until ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use <span class=\"strong\"> time clauses  </span>to link different clauses and events. Usually a<span class=\"strong\">  time clause</span> introduces a subordinate clause in relation to another event found in the main clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> every time </span> to talk about a main action that always happens when the subordinate action happens.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> Every time</span> you forget to phone in, the restaurant's reputation is at stake.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> once </span> when you want to say that something needs to happen for another event to occur.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Give me a call <span class=\"strong\"> once</span> you've decided.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> before </span> to talk about an action that happens before another action but doesn't necessarily last until the second action begins.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I was one of your best employees<span class=\"strong\">  before </span> any of this happened.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">until</span>  to talk about an action that happens before another action and lasts <span class=\"strong\"> until</span> the second action begins.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">That's why you three will be on probation<span class=\"strong\">  until </span> you've learned this lesson.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We have all gotten sick, but <span class=\"strong\"> before</span> I decide to stay home, I call in and let people know! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was one of your best employees <span class=\"strong\"> before</span> any of this happened.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get a little loose  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be more relaxed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have found that things are getting a little loose around here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when your boss is talking!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "back on point  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to focus on the task at hand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to get everyone back on point.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fender bender", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a minor collision between two vehicles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If  fender benders didn't happen, we would never be late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "busted their behinds ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work or be made to work very hard at completing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If the people here last night had not busted their behinds  the restaurant's reputation would have taken a big hit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "payday ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the day you receive your pay from your job", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We would miss out on big corporate paydays if staff didn't come to work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "first-rate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is extremely good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are first-rate to work with.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "In a group, brainstorm types of office conflicts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, create a 5 minute role-play of an office conflict situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Role-play your scenario.", "type": "text"}, {"con